schemaVersion: 1.0.0
manifest:
  id: oharness.example.mattpocock-skills
  name: Matt Pocock skills
  version: 0.1.0
  description: 'Bundled harness modelled on mattpocock/skills: setup, grill-with-docs, to-spec, to-tickets, implement (tdd), two-axis code-review, pr, human merge and retro. Source: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills.'
  license: MIT
  tags:
    - example
    - skills
    - tdd
    - mattpocock
graph:
  nodes:
    - data:
        consumes: []
        emits:
          - Repo configured
        label: setup-matt-pocock-skills
        providerIds: []
        roleId: setup
        systemPrompt: 'Run once per repo: ask which issue tracker to use, which triage labels apply, and where docs are saved.'
      id: setup
      position:
        x: 0
        y: 240
      type: agent
    - data:
        consumes:
          - Repo configured
        emits:
          - Aligned
        label: grill-with-docs
        providerIds: []
        roleId: griller
        systemPrompt: Grill the user about the change until every branch of the design tree is resolved, sharpening terms in GLOSSARY.md and recording ADRs inline.
      id: grill
      position:
        x: 280
        y: 240
      type: agent
    - data:
        label: grilling
        providerIds: []
        skillId: grilling
      id: grilling
      position:
        x: 280
        y: 0
      type: skill
    - data:
        label: domain-modeling
        providerIds: []
        skillId: domain-modeling
      id: domain-modeling
      position:
        x: 280
        y: 480
      type: skill
    - data:
        approvalLabel: Aligned
        label: Alignment
      id: alignment
      position:
        x: 560
        y: 240
      type: hitl
    - data:
        consumes: []
        emits:
          - Spec published
        label: to-spec
        providerIds: []
        roleId: spec-writer
        systemPrompt: Turn the conversation into a spec and publish it to the issue tracker. No new interview.
      id: to-spec
      position:
        x: 840
        y: 240
      type: agent
    - data:
        consumes:
          - Spec published
        emits:
          - Tickets ready
        label: to-tickets
        providerIds: []
        roleId: ticket-writer
        systemPrompt: Break the spec into tracer-bullet tickets, each declaring its blocking edges.
      id: to-tickets
      position:
        x: 1120
        y: 240
      type: agent
    - data:
        consumes:
          - Tickets ready
        emits:
          - Ready for review
        label: implement
        providerIds: []
        roleId: implementer
        systemPrompt: Build the tickets, driving /tdd at the pre-agreed seams, then close out with /code-review before committing.
      id: implement
      position:
        x: 1400
        y: 240
      type: agent
    - data:
        label: tdd
        providerIds: []
        skillId: tdd
      id: tdd
      position:
        x: 1400
        y: 0
      type: skill
    - data:
        label: codebase-design
        providerIds: []
        skillId: codebase-design
      id: codebase-design
      position:
        x: 1400
        y: 480
      type: skill
    - data:
        label: diagnosing-bugs
        providerIds: []
        skillId: diagnosing-bugs
      id: diagnosing-bugs
      position:
        x: 1120
        y: 0
      type: skill
    - data:
        checklist: Standards axis (repo standards + smell baseline) · Spec axis (matches the issue/spec) · run as parallel sub-agents · fail → back to implement
        consumes: []
        emits: []
        gateId: code-review
        label: code-review
      id: code-review
      position:
        x: 1680
        y: 240
      type: gate
    - data:
        consumes: []
        emits:
          - PR opened
        label: pr
        providerIds: []
        roleId: pr-writer
        systemPrompt: 'Write the PR body: smallest visual summary, before/after evidence, merge-danger call (one-way or two-way door, blast radius).'
      id: pr
      position:
        x: 1960
        y: 240
      type: agent
    - data:
        approvalLabel: Merge
        label: Human merge
      id: merge
      position:
        x: 2240
        y: 240
      type: hitl
    - data:
        consumes:
          - PR opened
        emits: []
        label: retro
        providerIds: []
        roleId: retro
        systemPrompt: After the session, suggest improvements to the agent's environment (navigation, checks, standards, steering files, tooling), most severe first.
      id: retro
      position:
        x: 2520
        y: 240
      type: agent
  edges:
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: configured
        signal: Repo configured
      id: e-setup-grill
      source: setup
      sourceHandle: out
      target: grill
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: skill
        signal: grilling
      id: e-grilling-grill
      source: grilling
      sourceHandle: out
      target: grill
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: skill
        signal: domain-modeling
      id: e-domain-modeling-grill
      source: domain-modeling
      sourceHandle: out
      target: grill
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: aligned
        signal: Aligned
      id: e-grill-alignment
      source: grill
      sourceHandle: out
      target: alignment
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: accept
        label: approve
      id: e-alignment-to-spec
      source: alignment
      sourceHandle: approve
      target: to-spec
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: spec
        signal: Spec published
      id: e-to-spec-to-tickets
      source: to-spec
      sourceHandle: out
      target: to-tickets
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: tickets
        signal: Tickets ready
      id: e-to-tickets-implement
      source: to-tickets
      sourceHandle: out
      target: implement
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: skill
        signal: tdd
      id: e-tdd-implement
      source: tdd
      sourceHandle: out
      target: implement
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: skill
        signal: codebase-design
      id: e-codebase-design-implement
      source: codebase-design
      sourceHandle: out
      target: implement
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: skill
        signal: diagnosing-bugs
      id: e-diagnosing-bugs-implement
      source: diagnosing-bugs
      sourceHandle: out
      target: implement
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: review
        signal: Ready for review
      id: e-implement-code-review
      source: implement
      sourceHandle: out
      target: code-review
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: accept
        label: pass
      id: e-code-review-pr
      source: code-review
      sourceHandle: pass
      target: pr
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: flow
        label: PR
        signal: PR opened
      id: e-pr-merge
      source: pr
      sourceHandle: out
      target: merge
      targetHandle: in
    - data:
        kind: accept
        label: merged
      id: e-merge-retro
      source: merge
      sourceHandle: approve
      target: retro
      targetHandle: in
content:
  prompts:
    OVERVIEW: |
      # Matt Pocock skills — bundled harness

      Source: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills ("Skills for Real Engineers"). The skills are small and composable; this
      harness chains the engineering ones the way the README describes them.

      Skills split by who invokes them. User-invoked skills orchestrate (setup-matt-pocock-skills,
      grill-with-docs, to-spec, to-tickets, implement, retro); model-invoked skills hold reusable
      discipline (grilling, domain-modeling, tdd, codebase-design, diagnosing-bugs, code-review, pr).
      A user-invoked skill may call model-invoked ones, never another user-invoked one.

      Flow:
      1. setup-matt-pocock-skills — once per repo: issue tracker, triage labels, docs location.
      2. grill-with-docs — align with the user (grilling) while building the shared language in
         GLOSSARY.md and ADRs (domain-modeling). The user confirms alignment.
      3. to-spec — publish the spec to the issue tracker.
      4. to-tickets — tracer-bullet tickets with blocking edges.
      5. implement — red-green-refactor via tdd at agreed seams; codebase-design keeps modules deep;
         diagnosing-bugs for hard bugs.
      6. code-review — two axes, Standards and Spec, as parallel sub-agents. A failing review goes
         back to implement (folded into the gate so the canvas graph stays acyclic).
      7. pr — PR body with evidence and merge-danger call; a human merges.
      8. retro — environment improvements after the session.

      For large work, `implement-spec` (subagents across the ticket frontier) and `wayfinder`
      (decision-ticket map) replace steps 4–5. Providers are left unset: pick them in the app.
  agents:
    griller: |
      # grill-with-docs

      Interview the user one question at a time until the plan is fully understood. Challenge vague terms against GLOSSARY.md, update it inline, and record hard-to-explain decisions as ADRs.
    implementer: |
      # implement

      Work the tickets in dependency order. Use red-green-refactor (tdd) at the pre-agreed seams, keep modules deep (codebase-design), and close out with code-review before committing.
    pr-writer: |
      # pr

      Write the pull request body: a summary as the smallest visual that makes the change clear, before/after evidence that it works, and a merge-danger call.
    retro: |
      # retro

      Review the session and suggest improvements to the coding agent's environment, most severe first.
    setup: |
      # setup-matt-pocock-skills

      Configure this repo for the engineering skills: ask which issue tracker to use (GitHub, GitLab, local files or other), which labels triage applies, and where docs are saved. Run once per repo.
    spec-writer: |
      # to-spec

      Synthesize what has already been discussed into a spec and publish it to the configured issue tracker. Ask which modules are touched; do not start a new interview.
    ticket-writer: |
      # to-tickets

      Break the spec into thin tracer-bullet tickets that each cut through every layer, and declare each ticket's blocking edges.
  skills:
    code-review: |
      # code-review

      Review the diff since a fixed point on two axes in parallel sub-agents: Standards and Spec. Report them side by side.
    codebase-design: |
      # codebase-design

      Design deep modules: a lot of behaviour behind a small interface, placed at a clean seam and tested through that interface.
    diagnosing-bugs: |
      # diagnosing-bugs

      Build a feedback loop that goes red on the bug, minimise, hypothesise, instrument, fix, then add a regression test.
    domain-modeling: |
      # domain-modeling

      Build and sharpen the project's domain model: challenge terms against the glossary, stress-test with edge cases, update GLOSSARY.md and ADRs.
    grilling: |
      # grilling

      The interview primitive: ask relentlessly about a plan, decision or idea until every branch of the design tree is resolved.
    tdd: |
      # tdd

      Red-green-refactor, one vertical slice at a time: write a failing test, make it pass, then refactor.
  hooks: {}
  commands:
    grill-with-docs: Grilling session that also updates GLOSSARY.md and ADRs.
    implement: Build the spec or tickets with tdd and code-review.
    retro: Suggest environment improvements after a session.
    setup-matt-pocock-skills: Configure the repo for the engineering skills.
    to-spec: Publish the current conversation as a spec.
    to-tickets: Split a spec into tracer-bullet tickets.
  scripts: {}
runtime:
  preferred: api
  cli:
  env: []
  secrets: []
validation:
  mockProfile: default
